DEVLOG — updates.txt fifth pass (08f10b4)

TWO SELF-INFLICTED BUGS from the previous pass, both worth remembering:

1. Sparkles froze. Fixing 'it looks like rain' by removing gravity, I
   replaced directed motion with damped Brownian noise: symmetric random
   impulses averaging zero, damped 0.97/frame. Net motion ~0. The lesson is
   that 'not rain' and 'not moving' are different requirements — the fix is a
   persistent per-particle HEADING with constant speed that slowly turns, so
   velocity is recomputed (never accumulated) and there is no shared axis.
   Test by diffing the canvas 1s apart, not by eye.

2. Find Me grew on hover. The fan was animating slot WIDTH 0 -> 2.6rem, which
   necessarily resizes the pill. Reserving width at rest and animating only
   opacity/translateY is what keeps the button a fixed size. The clip that
   makes icons look like they rise from below must live on an INNER mask —
   putting overflow:hidden on the slot also swallows the tooltip.

PLAY ME took three attempts because I kept raising LUMINANCE inside a warm
amber card. Brightness cannot separate an element from a bright background;
hue can. Cool panel + cyan border on the warm card finally worked. Reach for
hue contrast before brightness when something 'won't stand out'.

SIDE BEAMS in overlay mode wash over whatever is beneath them. The photo and
quote are lifted to z-40 (rays are z-30) so the beams only cross the text
column. If more content is added to the hero, decide per element whether it
should be above or below z-30.

